Part of the content discussed in #353.

**Problem.** `ConnectionHandler.onReconnect` is a TODO that answers every reconnect login (login type 18) with `ConnectFail`. When a client loses its connection for a moment (a network blip, or a mobile client the OS puts in the background), it tries to reconnect, gets "Unexpected server response" and goes back to the login screen. Meanwhile its player stays in the world for the grace period, so logging in again right away fails with "account still logged in". The grace period is 16 cycles (about 10 s), which is too short for a reconnect.

**Change.**
- `onReconnect` queues the request to the game thread (`AccountRegistry.queueReconnect`). Queued reconnects run at the start of `handleLogins`, before queued logins, and they don't count against the logins-per-cycle limit.
- New `PlayerReconnect` (api/net) looks for the online player whose current session's login seed equals the key the reconnect presents. If both logins carry a username, it must match too (case-insensitive). The reconnect is rejected (`ConnectFail`) when the player's logout is already under way or was requested. Otherwise the player moves to the new session:
  - the info protocols' `onReconnect()` is called;
  - the response is `ReconnectOk`;
  - the player gets a new `RspClient` on the same `Infos`;
  - `RspCycle.reconnect` swaps the session and re-assigns the build area and the npc view distance on the next update, with no rebuild packet (the client keeps its scene);
  - the disconnected flag and counter are reset, and the old session is closed.
- The disconnection hook (`PlayerReconnect.disconnectionHook`, used by `AccountLoadResponseHook` as well) marks the player disconnected only if the closing session is still the player's current one. So the old socket closing after a reconnect doesn't start a logout.
- New `SessionStateEvent.Reconnect`. `LoginScript` handles it by sending varps, stats and run energy again, and every transmitted inventory in full. Packets written while the connection was gone are lost.
- `RECONNECT_GRACE_PERIOD` goes from 16 to 100 cycles (60 s).
- `RspClient` exposes its `session` and `infos`. `api:net` and `api:registry` get `mockk` as a test dependency.

**Tests.**
- `PlayerReconnectTest` (5): seed matching, the username rule, no reconnect during a logout, and the disconnection hook for the current session vs. an old one.
- `AccountRegistryReconnectTest` (2): queued reconnects run once, outside the logins-per-cycle limit.

Checked in game on our build (rev 241):
- Desktop RuneLite: a server-side socket close gives "<name> reconnected (DESKTOP)". The player stays logged in, and inventory updates, walking and npcs work afterwards. A client frozen for about 24 s, past the 15 s idle close, reconnected when it resumed.
- Android client: 30 s in the background comes back in place.

Not re-checked in game on this branch.

**Data sources.** The 60 s grace period comes from the OSRS Wiki's "Logout button" page: "a 60 second timer before the game forcibly logs you out after an unexpected disconnection during combat".

**Caveats.**
- The wiki's 60 s is for disconnects during combat. Using it for every disconnect is a guess.
- Resending state after a reconnect is our choice. We don't know whether Jagex resends anything, but without the resend, changes made while the connection was gone never reach the client.
- **Not verified:** the Android case past 60 s. In a 90 s background test the client ended on the login screen. While the app is in the background, the Android client retries the reconnect every ~16 s, and we don't yet know why the later retries didn't hold the session. That case still needs a check.
- Only one reconnect can match a seed. A second reconnect with the same seed after a successful one finds nothing, because the player's session now has the new login's seed.

**Release note.** Players who lose their connection for up to a minute reconnect in place instead of going back to the login screen.

**Checklist**
- [x] The change compiles (`./gradlew build`).
- [x] Tests related to the change pass (`./gradlew assemble`, `test`, `integration`, `spotlessCheck`).
- [x] No documentation change needed.
- [x] No unrelated formatting or dependency changes (the test-only `mockk` dependency is new for `api:net` and `api:registry`).
- [x] Manual testing notes are under Tests above.

